4-602.13 The following nonfood contact surfaces were observed to be soiled:
A) inside butter topping storage cabinets (topping buildup/general debris);
B) under counter top equipment in food service area (dust/debris); 
C) steamer drip tray (food debris);
D) shelf above steamer (dust buildup);
E) bottom inside reach-in freezer in food service area (food crumbs); and
F) ledge under oven door (food debris).
Clean the aforementioned items.
Nonfood contact surfaces shall be cleaned at a frequency necessary to eliminate buildup of grease, food splash and general debris.
